// pfodWeb NOTE: excludes GPIO35-37/40-42/45 - dedicated onboard TFT
// display + SPI bus, GPIO7/21 - internal power-gate lines. Confirmed via
// vendor pins_arduino.h (MOSI=35,SCK=36,MISO=37,TFT_DC=40,TFT_RST=41,
// TFT_CS=42,TFT_BACKLITE=45,TFT_I2C_POWER=7,NEOPIXEL_POWER=21):
// https://github.com/espressif/arduino-esp32/blob/master/variants/adafruit_feather_esp32s2_reversetft/pins_arduino.h
// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO13 tagged "led_high" - confirmed active-high user
// LED (LED_BUILTIN=13; https://learn.adafruit.com/esp32-s2-reverse-tft-feather/pinouts
// - "labeled #13", active-high). GPIO33 tagged "led_neopixel" - confirmed
// onboard NeoPixel (PIN_NEOPIXEL=33, same pinouts page/pins_arduino.h).
// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO0/1/2 tagged "button" - CORRECTED (previously kept
// as plain GPIO with no button tag). This board has 3 real onboard
// pushbuttons D0/D1/D2 wired to GPIO0/1/2, confirmed via
// https://learn.adafruit.com/esp32-s2-reverse-tft-feather/pinouts :
// "Pushbutton D0 is D0/GPIO0, Pushbutton D1 is D1/GPIO1, Pushbutton D2 is
// D2/GPIO2." D0 doubles as the BOOT button (pulled HIGH, goes LOW when
// pressed); D1/D2 are plain inputs (pulled LOW, goes HIGH when pressed).
// Confirmed usable in application code (not just bootloader entry) via
// https://learn.adafruit.com/esp32-s2-reverse-tft-feather/digital-input-multiple-buttons
{
